What is Reconstructed Skin Models?
Reconstructed Skin Models are three dimensional, laboratory grown human epidermal and dermal constructs that replicate the architecture and barrier functions of native skin. These models are engineered to serve as platforms for toxicity testing, disease modelling, cosmetic safety evaluation, and regenerative medicine research, offering an ethical alternative to animal experiments while delivering physiologically relevant outcomes.
